{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-12313-r4587257","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Denver Crunch","sourcePageId":12313,"sourceRevision":"4587257","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-26T23:34:37Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Codename Noreste","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Denver%20Crunch&oldid=4587257","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:41:38.871Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cream cheese","Category:Recipes using fruit","Category:Recipes using powdered sugar","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes without cooking time"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"e19b67a1fb7eed4a000fa3c19c06d07753c12dd0df8b7dd3e86652cce06e03f8","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary|category=Recipes for dessert|servings=8|difficulty=3}}\n\n{{recipe}}| [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|United States]] | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Dessert]]\n\n'''Denver Crunch''' is a layered dessert that includes a crunchy base, a cream cheese middle, and a fruit top.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Crust ===\n*2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n*1 cup [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Pecan|pecans]]\n*2 cup [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n*1 cup [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n\n=== Filling ===\n*11 [[Cookbook:Oz|oz]] [[Cookbook:Cream Cheese|cream cheese]]\n*1 cup [[Cookbook:Powdered Sugar|powdered sugar]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]]\n*Fruit filling of choice\n\n==Procedure==\n\n=== Crust ===\n# Mix crust ingredients like pie crust until crumbly.\n# Press in [[Cookbook:Pie and Tart Pans|pan]]. [[Cookbook:Bake|Bake]] at 350°F until brown. Cool.\n# Take fork and crumble into small pieces. Some may be reserved for topping if you choose.\n\n=== Filling ===\n# [[Cookbook:Beating|Beat]] cream cheese, sugar, and vanilla until fluffy.\n# Spoon the filling on the crust until it is covered.\n# Top with your favorite fruit filling.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n\n* Thickened [[Cookbook:Blackberry|blackberries]] and [[Cookbook:Boysenberry|boysenberries]] make excellent toppings.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cream cheese]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fruit]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using powdered sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Denver Crunch","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cups flour","sourceText":"2 cups flour","amountText":"2 cups flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 cup chopped pecans","sourceText":"1 cup chopped pecans","amountText":"1 cup chopped pecans","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 cup brown sugar","sourceText":"2 cup brown sugar","amountText":"2 cup brown sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 cup butter","sourceText":"1 cup butter","amountText":"1 cup butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"11 oz cream cheese","sourceText":"11 oz cream cheese","amountText":"11 oz cream cheese","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 cup powdered sugar","sourceText":"1 cup powdered sugar","amountText":"1 cup powdered sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 tsp vanilla","sourceText":"1 tsp vanilla","amountText":"1 tsp vanilla","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"Fruit filling of choice","sourceText":"Fruit filling of choice","amountText":"Fruit filling of choice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Mix crust ingredients like pie crust until crumbly.","sourceText":"Mix crust ingredients like pie crust until crumbly.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Press in pan. Bake at 350°F until brown. Cool.","sourceText":"Press in pan. Bake at 350°F until brown. Cool.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Take fork and crumble into small pieces. Some may be reserved for topping if you choose.","sourceText":"Take fork and crumble into small pieces. Some may be reserved for topping if you choose.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Beat cream cheese, sugar, and vanilla until fluffy.","sourceText":"Beat cream cheese, sugar, and vanilla until fluffy.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Spoon the filling on the crust until it is covered.","sourceText":"Spoon the filling on the crust until it is covered.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":6,"text":"Top with your favorite fruit filling.","sourceText":"Top with your favorite fruit filling.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions h